*Solution Steps Walkthrough:*

1. Perform partial fraction decomposition on the factors involving $z^2$.
2. Factor out $z^2$ from the denominators to create terms of the form $1 / (1 - w)$ where $|w| < 1$ for $|z| > 2$.
3. Expand each term into its geometric power series in $1/z^2$.
4. Combine terms and include the factor $1 / (5 z)$.
